sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Client (signed in on the website)
    participant T as POST /api/auth/token
    participant J as JwtTokens
    participant A as /api endpoint (JWT bearer)
    participant DB as dbo.Users

    Note over C,T: Step 1 - get a token. Needs the website login cookie,<br/>so the email link and authenticator code already happened.
    C->>T: POST (login cookie)
    T->>DB: FindById(user id from cookie)
    DB-->>T: user (active?)
    alt cookie missing, or account inactive
        T-->>C: 302 to login / 401
    else
        T->>J: Create(user, key, now)
        J-->>T: HS256 token: sub, name, email, role, stamp<br/>iss, aud, exp = now + 15 min
        T-->>C: 200 { token, tokenType, expiresAt } - Cache-Control: no-store
    end

    Note over C,A: Step 2 - use it. The cookie is ignored on /api.
    C->>A: GET /api/... Authorization: Bearer token
    A->>A: signature, issuer, audience, expiry (30 s skew),<br/>algorithm pinned to HS256
    alt bad, tampered, expired or "alg: none"
        A-->>C: 401 (bare, no HTML error page)
    else token accepted
        A->>DB: FindById(sub)
        DB-->>A: user
        alt inactive, stamp changed (password), or role changed
            A-->>C: 401 - token refused
        else account unchanged
            A->>A: role policy (Any user / Staff / Admin)
            alt role not allowed
                A-->>C: 403
            else allowed
                A-->>C: 200 JSON (own orders: user id from token only)
            end
        end
    end
